-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-05: approved, timing fix to
              follow

  Replay      rework v2 as recorded on refactor-final f09750a (not repeated
              here; the rebuild = recorded, plain 02fd1835, sprites ec0706e9):
              both recordings IDENTICAL, 6,211 and 50,404 frames (412,000
              objects, 22.4M sprite pixels), the IM 1 handler equal to the
              original's at every menu interrupt against NextZXOS's ROM3; unit
              461 cases PASS, 3 negative controls + rom3_left + the old tail
              detected; ROM paths: every ROM byte as recorded; both start-up
              tails never read before written. Clock matrix not passed: every
              hook leaves at 3.5 MHz (NEXTREG 7,0), as Dean's engine is built;
              at 7 / 14 / 28 MHz in the exit would not be the incoming speed

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: the trophy screen after the title drawn
              clean (Dean's f0aecd13 shows it corrupted at the same frame),
              menus, walk-on scene, kick-off and the match, frames viewed;
              flicker 300 frames of the match: 0 out of step, 0 vanished, 0
              transients; 15-minute soak against the original .z80: no crash;
              both runs wait at the half-time menu (the profile never presses
              ENTER there), which the soak calls a freeze in the build only
              because its score differs; no person played it

  Coverage    first halves with the computer and player 1 on Kempston (random
              input); no second half, no 2-player game, no Match Day Special,
              no menu changes; no cheats (the archive's .pok has only value-
              asking entries); no loading screen (the tool adds its stub in
              the highest bank, and this build holds Sinclair's ROM in bank
              47)

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
